# Section C, candidate M1. Independent reading before the stored fields.
FG-M1-10ddb441f8 || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=implementer; act=typed exceptions for selected cases are a consistent project-level decision when used; trig=typed exceptions used; scope=error-handling rule, backend; exc=none; time=design; enf=text || test=Could mean: if used, use them consistently; or adopting them at all is a project-level decision; or a description of what approved typed exceptions are. API-011 only limits them as default architecture. Text does not say whether one local typed exception needs a decision.
FG-M1-30119e9885 || cls=XW mod=MUST dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=L || actor=harness and hook; act=block shell command on hook failure and tell user repair goes through template-maintenance; trig=hook failure; scope=pre-tool-use hook, settings; exc=none; time=PreToolUse; enf=hook code and declared onFailure, not executed || test=Oracle has no fail-closed duty. The code path exits 2 with a deny message. Effect on the real host is not established here.
FG-M1-39e2cd090f || cls=MX mod=REQUIRES_APPROVAL dom=MX rel=PE pol=GOV-017~,ARC-020~ conf=M || actor=agent and user; act=slot or declared-property change is Reserved, needs ADR; observable property must not change silently; user runs template-maintenance to apply; trig=capability selection change; scope=architecture-decision skill; exc=none; time=before and after approval; enf=text || test=Reserved routing overlaps GOV-017 and ARC-020. Slots and capability mechanics are candidate-specific instruction topology. ADR recording goes beyond. Three different outcomes.
FG-M1-430cbeb721 || cls=MX mod=MUST_NOT dom=WF rel=PE pol=GOV-015~,GOV-019~,GOV-020~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=listed Git operations only when requested or required by approved workflow, after inspecting; trig=high-risk Git; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=explicit request or approved workflow; time=before operation; enf=text || test=Explicit branch matches GOV-015, inspection matches GOV-020, approved-workflow branch stays open.
FG-M1-456f6c0b26 || cls=CD mod=MUST_NOT dom=WF rel=PE pol=GOV-015~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=treat main, master, protected or shared branches as non-rewritable; trig=history rewrite on those; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=semicolon-joined to the explicit-request sentence; time=before push; enf=text || test=Joined by a semicolon, so closer to the exception than in M. Exception reach still not stated; if no exception, stronger than GOV-015.
FG-M1-57aa941363 || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=implementer; act=invalidate before mutation success only when workflow deliberately accepts; trig=pre-success invalidation; scope=caching skill; exc=deliberate acceptance; time=design; enf=text || test=Same open question on RUN-021's phrase as M.
FG-M1-6a3f471ef0 || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=agent; act=destructive Git only when requested or required by approved workflow; trig=destructive Git; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=approved workflow; time=before operation; enf=text || test=Same open question on GOV-015 as M. This wording reads as a limit (only when), and is not a permission as in M's claim, though it is the same source sentence.
FG-M1-6a4037ede3 || cls=XW mod=MUST dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=harness; act=run pre-tool-use before every Bash or PowerShell call to gate dependency and reference commands; trig=each shell call; scope=settings.json; exc=none; time=PreToolUse; enf=declared hook, not executed || test=Adds a gate on every shell call. The oracle states the dependency duties but not this gate. Host semantics of args and onFailure not established.
FG-M1-701faea2b7 || cls=XW mod=MUST dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=L || actor=hook; act=block when payload lacks tool name; trig=malformed input; scope=pre-tool-use hook; exc=none; time=PreToolUse; enf=hook code, not executed || test=Implementation detail of the fail-closed path. Whether it occurs on the real host is unknown. Fact about the same mechanism as FG-M1-30119e9885.
FG-M1-a740c4fdf7 || cls=CD mod=MUST_NOT dom=WF rel=PE pol=DEP-003~ conf=M || actor=checker; act=floating or empty versions are errors with no explicit-request exception; prerelease is a warning; ranges not flagged; trig=checker runs; scope=check-manifests script; exc=none for floating; time=when invoked; enf=script finding, not executed || test=DEP-003 allows floating on request; checker errors regardless. Narrower elsewhere (ranges pass). Add-dependency says do not use floating with no exception too, which is a text-level stronger claim as well.
FG-M1-d746992071 || cls=UN mod=UNCERTAIN dom=UN rel=UN pol=- conf=L || actor=agent; act=are protected branches non-rewritable even with explicit force-push authorization; trig=explicit request to rewrite main; scope=git-workflow skill; exc=the explicit-request sentence; time=before push; enf=text || test=Sentence one allows force-push of a shared branch on request; sentence two treats main and shared branches as non-rewritable. Since shared appears in both, an unconditional second sentence would empty the first. Harmonized reading: non-rewritable is the standing default, explicit request remains the route. But main is singled out, and could be read as absolute.
FG-M1-e3684cb036 || cls=MX mod=MUST dom=MX rel=PE pol=GOV-017~,ARC-020~ conf=M || actor=agent and hook; act=reference-graph change is Reserved; commands denied until project-structure applied, marker re-run; other project-file changes reported for confirmation; trig=project reference change; scope=hook, project-structure, CLAUDE.md; exc=branch switch needs no workflow; time=before and after commands; enf=hook, not executed || test=Reserved status matches ARC-020 new layers and GOV-017, though reference graph is not named. Denial and marker protocol are executable extras. Confirmation reminder is another extra. Distinct outcomes.
